troke cases, they are not considered outliers.\"\n    # So for each observation that is an outlier (by IQR), look at other observations (in the dataset) that share the same glucose value. If 50%+ of those *other* observations have stroke=1, then this observation is NOT an outlier.\n    # So the group is defined by the exact value. \"Other observations\" — meaning all other observations in the dataset that have that same value (other than maybe the current one being evaluated). Or just count over all observations with that value. That’s usually how it’s interpreted.\n    pass\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
