timestamp=2026-11-04T19:42:19.264Z level=INFO run=ebc6dc18 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# check our thresholds: age of children <= 14, age of toddlers <= 3\n# cases like age 9,11,12,13 with work_type children and smoker - we marked as outlier by (is_smoke_group and age <= 14) OR (is_smoke_group and work == 'children'). Both true. Also (age <= 3 and 'student' in work) gives idx 52 (age 1.8, student, formerly smoked) - marked. That matches \"toddlers that are students\".\n# Also note: the rule says \"values among the categorical variables that are unlikely in reality, such as “smoker” or “formerly smoked” / person working in children.\" Another interpretation is smoking status is “smoker” or “formerly smoked” while being a child (or working as child)? Yes matches. Also \"additionally you should check whether there are any toddlers that are students. If so they should be also considered as outliers.\"\n# Also \"For outlier detection in categorical variables, the age of children should be set to no more than 14. For outlier detection in categorical variables, the age of toddelrs should be set to no more than 3.\" - these thresholds are given as context for categorical outlier detection. So our logic aligns.\npass\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
